ond of its three goals wasn't done. The investigation work itself is good.\n\n**What holds up**\n- **Goal 1 (200 docs × 5 clients gave no result):** the cause is well supported. The test script never sends `unLockDocument`, so after 30 s (`expire.lockDoc`) the server drops the first editor. The script's wait for `saveLock` has no timeout, so it hangs. This fits the numbers: 100 × 10 opened in under 30 s, while 200 docs took 38–110 s to open. After the fix, 1,000 and 2,000 sockets ran with no errors. The only limit noted is that the load generator shares the server's 2 CPUs.\n- **Goal 3 (124 s pptx → pdf conversion):** explained convincingly. The converter runs one job at a time (`maxprocesscount` 1) and save assembly uses the same queue. On an idle server 10 runs took 2.0–2.8 s; started right after a load test, the third run took 68.7 s. It also fits that deck-50 was the first file converted after PKT-0018's load test. The executor says plainly that PKT-0018's own logs no longer exist, so that last step is inferred, not checked.\n- **Bookkeeping:** the Executor log is filled in, both follow-ups are listed under Spawned packets and exist in `.theseus/spawn/`, the friction line is present, and the diff (4 files, 151 lines) is within budget.\n- **Scope:** the target file list, contract and acceptance commands are still template placeholders (`\"[FILE]\"`, `\"[WHAT MUST NOT CHANGE]\"`, no commands). Keeping changes to the packet, spawn requests and friction was the right call, but it means none of this was proven by an acceptance command.\n\n**Why it's rejected**\n- **Goal 2 is not done.** The goal asks for valid saves under load (callback status 2 instead of 3) and timed save assembly. Every save still returns status 3, even one change on a blank docx. The 138–143 s save timings only measure saves that fail. The executor says this themselves, and the rules say to reject when a goal requirement was not done.\n\n**What would let it pass**\nEither of these:\n1. Implement valid saves under load (the browser-captured change sequence already requested as a spawn), then time save assembly with status 2 callbacks.\n2. Formally narrow PKT-0021's goal to items 1 and 3 and move item 2 into its own packet. The spawn request for it already exists.\n\nEither way, the packet's target files, contract and acceptance commands should be filled in rather than left as template placeholders.\n\nVERDICT: REJECT Goal (2) not done (saves still return status 3, so save assembly timing is meaningless); implement it, or narrow the goal to items 1 and 3 and move item 2 to its own packet, and fill in the placeholder target, contract and acceptance.","ttft_ms":2305,"type":"result","duration_ms":16618,"uuid":"081cb095-ab99-4c04-9cf5-19692bbd3d51","ttft_stream_ms":1504,"time_to_request_ms":348,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":8,"system_prompt":170,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":20,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":26,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":10,"init_frame_send":5,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":3,"request_announcements":17,"query_setup":5,"auto_mode_context_wait":9,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":36,"message_normalization":4,"client_creation":7,"request_build":14},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":85,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":223,"time_to_request_major_faults":6,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":217,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":141,"process_rss_mib_result":224,"process_anon_mib_result":134,"process_peak_rss_mib":261,"process_cpu_ms_turn":1040,"process_wall_ms_turn":16618,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":368,"process_wall_ms_streaming":12688,"main_stream_count":4,"main_stream_event_count":258,"main_stream_chunk_count":77,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":7,"cpu_ms":21,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_sta